WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.240
"Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness"
finds Doctor Strange and the Scarlet Witch

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.690
sharing more screen time than ever before,
but what's their MCU relationship all about?

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.090
And what's different in the comics?

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:16.750
Spoilers for "Multiverse of Madness" ahead!

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:20.769
Doctor Strange and the Scarlet Witch began
their MCU tenure in an oddly similar fashion

00:00:20.769 --> 00:00:25.109
–- introduced in the same film, and through
the same organization.

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:29.499
Strange's first appearance was in name only,
during "Captain America: The Winter Soldier,"

00:00:29.499 --> 00:00:35.219
when Cap, Falcon, and Black Widow force double-agent
Jasper Sitwell to confess who HYDRA is targeting.

00:00:35.219 --> 00:00:39.260
"Bruce Banner, Stephen Strange, anyone who
is a threat to HYDRA."

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:43.530
Scarlet Witch is also introduced in "Winter
Soldier," in the film's mid-credits scene.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:47.679
Moving through a HYDRA base, Baron Strucker
tells a scientist about the organization's

00:00:47.679 --> 00:00:52.890
many experiments, finally revealing their
greatest success: the twins Quicksilver and

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.179
Scarlet Witch.

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:59.039
The siblings are far from the confident, composed
Avengers they would one day become, but it's

00:00:59.039 --> 00:01:02.640
clear nonetheless the innate power they possess.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.430
By the end of "Winter Soldier," both Doctor
Strange and Scarlet have officially entered

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:13.439
the MCU, in both cases through HYDRA agents
discussing their grand plans.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:18.180
Perhaps the biggest difference between Doctor
Strange and the Scarlet Witch is the source

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.159
and style of magic they wield.

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:25.290
Though both are world-class wizards, the two
climbed to that peak from opposite sides of

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.119
the magical mountain.

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:30.930
Strange spent his first few decades in an
entirely magic-less world.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:35.979
"I do not believe in fairytales about chakras
or energy or the power of belief.

00:01:35.979 --> 00:01:38.790
There is no such thing as spirit!"

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:43.909
It was only after a period of intense study
and practice that Strange learned to wield

00:01:43.909 --> 00:01:47.780
magic, and the magic itself reflects that
organized effort.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:51.240
As Kevin Feige told Comicbook.com of Strange's
magic,

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:03.970
Feige also compared Strange's orderly magic
with Wanda's, noting that while Strange learned

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:09.330
as an adult to write in the, quote, "source
code that shapes reality," Wanda gets introduced

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:13.209
to this unfathomable and inexplicable power,
forcing her to spend her whole adult life

00:02:13.209 --> 00:02:17.700
trying to control its chaos, or work within
it.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:22.310
Strange and Wanda both share one critically
important facet in their magical development:

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:23.849
an Infinity Stone.

00:02:23.849 --> 00:02:28.370
In "Doctor Strange," the character is forced
into a rushed curriculum, graduating to Master

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:33.380
of the Mystic Arts somewhat by default when
Kaecilius' attacks warranted his conscription

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:34.629
into the war.

00:02:34.629 --> 00:02:39.659
Likewise, Wanda was never formally educated,
merely poked and prodded by scientists in

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:45.360
between periods of self-study — as a child
in Sokovia and afterwards at the Avengers

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.360
Compound.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:51.769
Yet both received exponential magnifications
of their powers through connection to an Infinity

00:02:51.769 --> 00:02:52.769
Stone.

00:02:52.769 --> 00:02:56.930
At Kamar-Taj, Strange began experimenting
with the Eye of Agamotto, later revealed to

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:58.420
house the Time Stone.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:02.670
His proficiency with the artifact led to him
becoming its keeper, and he leaned on its

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:07.129
power arguably as much as he did every other
spell in his repertoire.

00:03:07.129 --> 00:03:12.269
Likewise, HYDRA used the Mind Stone to amplify
Wanda's powers and channel them into a more

00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:13.909
manipulatable form.

00:03:13.909 --> 00:03:19.450
Like Wanda's power in general, the exact nature
of the Mind Stone's influence is unknown,

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:25.290
but "WandaVision" made it clear that the Stone
helped lead Wanda to her ultimate destiny.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:30.950
The next in the long string of parallels between
Strange and Wanda is the nature of their heroism

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:33.590
and their place in superhero society.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:38.840
Unlike the MCU's more main-stage heroes such
as Captain America, Iron Man, and Thor, neither

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:43.319
Wanda nor Strange have ever fit in with the
core Avengers crowd.

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:47.260
Strange's relationship with the Avengers is
a relatively straightforward one.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:52.390
Strange has never been an Avenger, and what's
more, during "Infinity War," Stark makes Spider-Man

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:58.340
an official Avenger right in front of Strange
and never offers the sorcerer the same status.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:02.500
Though Wanda did become an official Avenger
at the end of "Age of Ultron," her tenure

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:06.159
was brief and marked by active opposition
to the group.

00:04:06.159 --> 00:04:10.629
Before joining the team, she actively fought
against them, first protesting against their

00:04:10.629 --> 00:04:14.760
presence in Sokovia and then joining Ultron's
campaign against them.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:19.640
And though she joined the Avengers in 2015's
"Age of Ultron," she left by 2016's "Captain

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:20.850
America: Civil War."

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:25.700
Fighting against Iron Man's registered Avengers,
she became a fugitive from the law and then

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:26.720
a prisoner.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.840
Her subsequent enslavement of an entire town
in New Jersey during "WandaVision" certainly

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:35.180
didn't help her case for reentry into the
group.

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:40.290
Though the two spellcasters never met during
"Infinity War," both participated in the defense

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:45.150
of Earth and its Infinity Stones in similar
conflicts, with each protecting their associated

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.091
Stone from pairs of Black Order enforcers.

00:04:47.091 --> 00:04:53.270
In New York City, Strange fought alongside
Stark, Wong, and Spider-Man against the formidable

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:56.120
duo of Cull Obsidian and Ebony Maw.

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:01.140
His only goal was to protect the Time Stone
from falling into the wrong hands, which he

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:02.830
accomplished — for a time.

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:07.410
Similarly, Wanda fought alongside Vision,
Cap, Black Widow, and Falcon against the duo

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.790
of Proxima Midnight and Corvus Glaive.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:15.400
Her only goal was to protect the Mind Stone
and the android whose head it was lodged in,

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.740
which she also accomplished –- for a time.

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:23.620
Both moved on to further battles, with Strange
fighting on Titan and Wanda fighting in Wakanda.

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:28.700
In both of their cases, the two sorcerers
ended up coming face to face with Thanos himself,

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:32.780
matching their might in one-on-one contests
with the Mad Titan.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:38.770
For both Strange and Wanda, their "Infinity
War" encounters with Thanos ended with grim,

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:45.110
pragmatic choices that forced both to voluntarily
lose that which they coveted the most.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:49.630
Throughout the film, Strange repeatedly expressed
his commitment to safeguarding the Time Stone

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:50.730
at any cost.

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:58.370
"If it comes to saving you or the kid or the
Time Stone, I will not hesitate to let either

00:05:58.370 --> 00:05:59.370
of you die."

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:03.420
Then, after searching millions of futures
to find the key to defeating Thanos, Strange

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.770
voluntarily hands him the Stone.

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:10.300
Even the relative certainty of his divination
could not have made Strange's decision an

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:14.130
easy one — especially knowing he would be
snapped out of existence.

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:18.820
Wanda, too, was forced to concede the Stone
she had so adamantly protected.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:23.380
In her case, however, the decision was even
more heart-wrenching and desperate, as the

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:28.260
Stone sat within the skull of Vision, the
man she loved, and her only recourse was to

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:29.690
destroy it.

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:34.620
Through bitter tears, Wanda succeeded, fragmenting
the Stone and killing Vision.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:40.600
As if her trauma was not enough, Thanos then
used the Time Stone to undo the entire sequence

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.120
of events.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:47.900
When "Infinity War" ended, both Strange and
Wanda were gone, snapped by Thanos into dust.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:52.130
Though both had played their parts admirably,
they had failed to prevent Thanos from accomplishing

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:53.200
his goal.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:58.440
Both were fated to make their grand return
as Act III of "Avengers: Endgame" commenced.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:02.970
Snapped back into existence by the Hulk, both
fought in the Battle of Earth against Thanos

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:04.800
and his armies.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:07.850
"You took everything from me."

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:10.766
"I don't even know who you are."

00:07:10.766 --> 00:07:12.710
"You will."

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:17.630
Strange helped shield the entire battlefield
from the destructive cannons of Thanos' flagship,

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:22.110
and single-handedly held back a flood that
threatened to drown the heroes.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:27.160
Wanda, inflamed with rage at the death of
Vision, used her powers to assault Thanos

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:32.720
head-on and even proved herself the stronger
power as she shattered the Titan's blade,

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:36.980
fractured his armor, and nearly crushed him
to death.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:42.310
One of the most tenuous but ultimately tantalizing
links between Strange and Wanda involves the

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:47.910
ancient spell tome known as the Darkhold and
its possible existence throughout Marvel movies

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:49.370
and TV shows.

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:54.310
It began in "Doctor Strange," when multiple
fans noticed one important spellbook noticeably

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:55.310
absent.

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:59.230
Then, when the infamous Darkhold appeared
in "Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.," fans connected

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:01.240
the conspicuous dots.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:05.990
The book appeared again in "WandaVision,"
when Agatha Harkness used its secrets to enhance

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:07.630
her own sorcery.

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:13.010
Forging a chain from all these links, we reach
the most likely conclusion that the Darkhold

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:17.770
was stolen from the library at Kamar-Taj where
Strange studied and found its way to Harkness,

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:21.030
who used it to manipulate Wanda during "WandaVision."

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:25.700
When last we saw Wanda before "Multiverse
of Madness," she was studying the book's dark,

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:31.330
ancient secrets, making it clear that Strange
would either find the book or detect its influence

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:32.880
on Wanda.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:36.750
Strange's second movie, "Doctor Strange in
the Multiverse of Madness," sees the good

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:40.440
doctor and the Scarlet Witch in direct conflict
for the first time.

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:45.440
Having delved deeply into the Darkhold, Wanda
begins the film under the book's insidious

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:46.440
influence.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:47.440
"The multiverse.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:48.440
It's dangerous."

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:55.690
She is cold, cruel, and wildly violent, and
she brings all of that wickedness to the forefront

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:59.940
in her quest to capture America Chavez and
steal the young woman's ability to travel

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:01.160
the multiverse.

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:07.270
Her success would mean Chavez's death, the
death of another universe's Wanda, and potentially

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:13.880
even the collapse of the entire multiverse,
and naturally, that doesn't fly with Strange.

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:19.260
The two wage a magical war across realities,
with Strange giving his all to protect the

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:22.330
multiverse, Chavez, and even Wanda herself.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.440
"This is going to be fun."

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:28.940
Ultimately, the Witch's quest leads to her
ruin, and in the process, the partial corruption

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:34.950
of Strange, as well – the film's final shot
is Strange, on his knees, struck with pain,

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:39.970
and bearing the creepy third eye that we last
saw on the evil version of Strange corrupted

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:44.590
by the Darkhold, but in the comics this would
be a physical manifestation of the Eye of

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:45.590
Agamotto.

00:09:45.590 --> 00:09:49.950
In the comics, one recurring theme between
the two is the doctor/patient relationship,

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:54.760
which makes sense given Strange's medical
degree and former career, and makes even more

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:58.930
sense given Strange's comprehensive knowledge
of all things arcane.

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:03.890
The pairing of Strange's two fields of expertise
makes him uniquely suited to handle ailments

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:09.280
when it comes to fellow magical beings, and
Wanda is no exception.

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:14.410
Strange was on hand in "Vision and the Scarlet
Witch" #12 to deliver Wanda's twin baby boys.

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:18.960
He was also the most effective at treating
Wanda's psychosis in "Avengers: Disassembled,"

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:22.720
understanding her reality-manipulating symptoms
better than any.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:27.310
Though his choice of treatment in the latter
and its follow-up "House of M" arguably did

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:33.510
as much harm as they did good, his strategy
was nonetheless the most informed of anyone's.

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:38.580
The most common form that Strange and Wanda's
relationship takes is that of mentor and mentee.

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:43.900
Strange is more experienced than Wanda, more
educated, and more in control of his powers,

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:48.360
largely due to his access to magical materials
and manuscripts that remained hidden throughout

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:49.880
Wanda's formative years.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:55.140
A telling recent example came in the miniseries
"Empyre: X-Men," in which one of Wanda's attempts

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:57.430
at atonement backfires.

00:10:57.430 --> 00:11:02.190
In attempting to undo her "no more mutants"
spell, in which she de-powered millions of

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:07.590
mutants at once, Wanda cast a spell to revive
the millions of mutants slain during the Massacre

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:08.590
at Genosha.

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:16.040
Instead, she raised an army of mutant zombies,
millions in number and still semi-superpowered.

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:20.430
Strange was able to undo the wayward spell,
but not without taking multiple occasions

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:25.660
to lecture Wanda on her misuse of magic and
lack of thorough training.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:30.410
The most recent relationship to form between
Strange and Wanda is that of a coworker.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:35.670
In the ongoing series "Strange Academy," Strange
created a school for magically- and supernaturally-adept

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:39.120
children to harness their innate gifts and
study their craft.

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:45.060
The school accepts students from all walks
of life, death, and undeath, and so Strange

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:49.180
hired a faculty even more varied and powerful
than their pupils.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:54.279
In issue #2, we learn that Wanda teaches a
course for which she is uniquely qualified,

00:11:54.279 --> 00:11:56.930
known as "Elements of Chaos Magic."

00:11:56.930 --> 00:12:01.380
The official course description lists Wanda
as "the foremost practitioner of the most

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:02.840
volatile magic."

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:07.650
Alongside professors more accustomed to the
orderly side of magic, as well as elemental

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:13.410
sorcerers like Magik and Daimon Hellstrom,
Wanda rounds out the academy's staff well.

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:18.360
Even more valuable is her experience in the
dangers of uncontrolled emotions and using

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:20.430
magic as an anesthetic.

